WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.929 --> 00:00:04.096
(hooting)

00:00:04.839 --> 00:00:08.110
(upbeat positive music)

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.840
- Hi there, I'm Aria, and we're here to spend a night

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:11.840
with the Juggalos.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:12.673
Come on in.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.440
^We'll go right down in here.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:16.383
No.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:22.290
^For those unaware, Juggalos are fans of the hip hop duo

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.420
^Insane Clown Posse, and they're a passionate community

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.853
^known for having their own unique culture.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.900
^From wearing face paint to spraying the soft drink Faygo

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.390
^at concerts, Juggalos have often been met with ridicule,

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.410
with the FBI even going as far as

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.263
to controversially classify them as a gang.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.023
So to try and separate fact from fiction,

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.280
I decided to spend the night at an ICP concert

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:48.873
to experience firsthand what it means to be a juggalo.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:50.440
What does this tattoo symbolize?

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.140
- [Dennis] That's a hatchet man, that just means

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.870
that we're down with the clown.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.760
- What does it mean to be down with the clown?

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:56.800
- To be down with the clown,

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.090
well for one we're not a gang.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.660
Don't matter if you're black, white, yellow, purple,

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.170
it don't matter, you find love.

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:05.003
- From what I understand, there is juggalo slang.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.080
- If you're a juggalo and they see you walking

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.020
and you got some of the material on,

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.800
you'll get a "woop woop," and that's a sign of respect.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.460
- Let's say I'm wearing some ICP merch,

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.610
let's simulate a situation, so I'm walking.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.500
- Woop woop, family!

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:20.830
Right, and that's all we do.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.180
- [Aria] After I eventually find my press pass,

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.450
I'm able to meet up with the Paulis brothers,

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:28.333
who are VIP ticket holders for tonight's show.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:29.590
- Is it too late to paint your face?

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:30.530
You gotta go find somebody,

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:31.780
there's always somebody with face paint.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:33.420
It's just not the same without the face paint.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.573
- [Aria] Despite being decades-long fans of ICP,

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.490
tonight will mark the very first time they're actually able

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:43.180
to meet the duo and spray Faygo with them on stage.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:45.650
- It's one of my life's ambitions and my life dreams,

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:47.623
like after the first show I was like,

00:01:48.147 --> 00:01:49.967
"I'm never gonna be a dope rapper,

00:01:49.967 --> 00:01:52.853
"but one day I will be up there, I will be throwing soda.

00:01:52.947 --> 00:01:56.797
"I will be, you know, doing that, I wanna do that."

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.800
And that stayed with me for the past 15, 20 years.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.400
- You guys are generally very, very friendly people.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:04.483
I mean which is interesting.

00:02:04.483 --> 00:02:05.316
- We try to be.

00:02:05.316 --> 00:02:06.149
It's fascinating because you know,

00:02:06.149 --> 00:02:07.450
if I was walking down the street,

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:09.600
and you guys were walking with this face paint...

00:02:11.107 --> 00:02:12.920
- Well yeah, I mean, because we're wearing corse paint,

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.270
^we look like f***ing weirdos, but I mean...

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.320
Yeah, I would avoid you, too, but anybody who's going

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.320
to a show obviously looks like a weirdo,

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.163
we're just a little bit more pronounced in that fact.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.150
- The people that are there for the music

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:26.400
and there for the right reason,

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.150
those are the people that I call family.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:29.880
Those are my Juggalos, those are my people.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.910
So, it's, you know, a couple bad apples spoil

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.493
the whole bunch unfortunately.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:35.973
- I think you could say that's the case

00:02:35.973 --> 00:02:37.580
for any community or culture.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.420
- That could be for anybody, from, you know,

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.030
the furries to the...

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.450
- To Michael Buble fans.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:43.590
- Yeah, to Michael Buble fans.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.380
They're the worst, man, they got shifts,

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:47.030
because they don't check the old ladies' purses.

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:50.030
- Some of the songs have a little bit of weird, racy content

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.470
but at the end of the day, it does have a positive message,

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:55.840
you just have to kind of get through the whole thing,

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.490
but going through the entire journey

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:00.503
is half of what made being a Juggalo fun.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.010
- [Aria] I then chat with Tim, who is also

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:06.150
moments away from meeting ICP for the first time.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.360
^So how excited are you?

00:03:07.672 --> 00:03:10.633
^- Um, less excited, more nervous.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.133
ICP kinda preaches, like if you're bullied,

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.630
if your life sucks, you know, all that stuff,

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.197
ICP comes out with their music and they're like,

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:22.060
"hey, our life sucks too, so let's suck lives together."

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:24.173
And they have a song, Simple and Blunt,

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.500
there's a line specifically that says,

00:03:26.927 --> 00:03:29.577
"let us do the killing for you, you'll be all right."

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.550
And it's not like actual killing,

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:32.427
it's more like a metaphor, like,

00:03:32.427 --> 00:03:37.427
"hey, let us be angry, let us do all that bad stuff.

00:03:38.087 --> 00:03:39.187
"You'll be fine."

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:42.230
- [Aria] Before the VIP meet-and-greet begins,

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:44.100
I'm actually able to sit down with

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.140
Insane Clown Posse themselves to learn more about

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.700
this massive community they've built over the years.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:52.287
- We say if somebody comes up to you and says,

00:03:52.287 --> 00:03:55.087
"hey man, I was gonna kill myself,

00:03:55.087 --> 00:03:57.787
"but your music saved my life."

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.470
And they take their f***ing shirt off, and their

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:01.853
whole back is a tattoo of your face,

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:03.190
you know what I'm saying?

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:04.777
How do you say thank you to that?

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:06.970
"Hey, thanks, guy." That don't cover it.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:09.487
- Believe it or not, they look us in the face and say,

00:04:09.487 --> 00:04:12.267
"you saved my life, your music saved my life."

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:16.623
That type of appreciation from them, for us,

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.333
for us doing something we love doing,

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:24.253
and we would f***ing do anything to be able to do this,

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.933
and then to be appreciated like that for it,

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.000
it's almost unfathomable.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.320
- You couldn't ask for a better fan base or

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.780
better people in the world, you know what I'm saying?

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.963
People from outside look in, make fun of them,

00:04:34.963 --> 00:04:36.970
call them white trash, call them piece of s**t,

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:39.380
uneducated, all that, couldn't be further from the truth.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.553
It's the most warmest, openest.

00:04:41.833 --> 00:04:44.380
From doctors to homeless people, you know what I'm saying?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.330
The whole spectrum, just like life.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.980
Juggalos cover the whole A to Z.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:49.180
- What should I be ready for tonight?

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.320
- We always tell somebody that ain't never seen us before,

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:53.517
we're like, "hey man, sorry to tell you this,

00:04:53.517 --> 00:04:55.430
"I gotta apologize right now because

00:04:55.587 --> 00:04:58.002
"you ever see somebody else, we're f***ing it up for you."

00:04:58.002 --> 00:04:58.835
You know what I'm saying, because you're never gonna

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.350
f***ing see no show like us ever again.

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:04.293
- [Aria] Michael Buble is ruined for me now?

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.213
- Everybody, Michael f***ing Budwol,

00:05:05.213 --> 00:05:06.720
whatever the f*** his name is.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.320
- Thank you guys so much, I'm looking forward to it.

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:10.400
- Thank you my man.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.250
- Thank you, can we have a group hug?

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:16.063
- Yeah, hell yeah!

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:19.623
- I wish he wasn't here so I could get your full arms.

00:05:20.392 --> 00:05:22.892
(light music)

00:05:24.172 --> 00:05:25.005
- How you doing, brother?

00:05:25.005 --> 00:05:25.930
- Doing well, how are you guys?

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:26.763
- Good man.

00:05:26.763 --> 00:05:28.030
^- I'm doing a lot better now.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:32.513
- Uh, no words, it's 22 years in the making.

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:34.199
- What do you do for a living,

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:35.383
you look like a doctor or something, right?

00:05:35.383 --> 00:05:37.940
- No, close, I work with the

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.010
handicapped community, actually.

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:39.843
- See?

00:05:39.843 --> 00:05:42.863
- I'm just rambling, no words, it's awesome, I'm just happy.

00:05:44.332 --> 00:05:45.165
- I'm happy you're happy.

00:05:45.165 --> 00:05:46.023
- Yeah, no words.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:48.750
- I'm so geeked right now, thank you guys.

00:05:49.703 --> 00:05:51.480
It was probably 40 percent more embarrassing

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:52.540
than I thought it was gonna be.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.930
Obviously Jay and Shaggy are cool as f***

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:57.193
and they made it special just for me.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:59.440
As an awkward, total neck beard weirdo

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:01.727
walking up to them like, "what's up bro?"

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:03.393
And they made it cool, they made it,

00:06:05.702 --> 00:06:08.640
Ugh, I got no words, I literally cannot describe

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:11.360
how geeked out I am about meeting the clowns

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:12.450
and shaking their hands.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:13.333
Oh my God.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:15.670
And now you get to watch them perform.

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.720
- [Aria] But before the concert starts,

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:21.083
there's one final thing that I need to take care of.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:26.880
- ICP!

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:30.853
- [Aria] Coming into tonight, I had no idea what to expect.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.250
But that's the thing about misconceptions, isn't it?

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:35.940
Because in general we often have a tendency

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:39.103
to allow the negative to overshadow all the good.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:41.713
We see these face painted people listening to this

00:06:41.713 --> 00:06:45.480
intense, dark music, and we allow ourselves to forget

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.750
that these are just regular people that have

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.083
found something that makes them happy.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:53.070
At the end of the day, we all just wanna

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.023
feel like we belong somewhere,

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.890
and that's what Juggalos have found in each other.

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.420
They come from all walks of life,

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.973
yet have been brought together through the music.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.263
There's something wonderful about that.

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:09.133
You'll often hear Juggalos refer to themselves as a family,

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:12.743
and tonight, I genuinely felt like I was one of them.

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:17.583
So woop, woop, because I'm down with the clown.

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:23.313
- [Dennis] I just turned 40 two days ago on March 20th.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:24.260
- [Aria] Happy belated birthday!

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:25.153
- [Dennis] Thank you very much.

00:07:25.153 --> 00:07:30.153
♪ Happy birthday to you, happy birthday, dear Dennis! ♪

